Position Overview
Kiewit is seeking a Project Engineer to support the execution of utility-scale power delivery projects, including transmission, distribution, and substation construction. This field-based role works closely with Superintendents, Project Managers, clients, and craft teams to ensure projects are safely executed on schedule, within budget, and in accordance with quality standards.District Overview

Kiewit Power Delivery is a full-service engineering and construction solutions provider, completing projects of all sizes and complexity. Across North America, our experience spans all transmission and distribution market aspects from high-voltage overhead and underground transmission to distribution design, automation design and construction capabilities. With these broad capabilities, we operate in the electric utility, renewable energy, industrial, and oil and gas markets.
Location
West Lake, TexasResponsibilities

Field Engineering & Construction Support

Support daily construction activities on transmission, distribution, and substation projects.
Work closely with field supervision to ensure work is performed according to plans, specifications, and project requirements.
Assist with work planning, means and methods, and construction sequencing.

Project Coordination

Coordinate material deliveries, equipment, subcontractors, and project resources.
Track and manage RFIs, design changes, submittals, and project documentation.
Support communication between engineering, field operations, and clients.

Schedule & Cost Control

Assist with project scheduling, progress tracking, and production reporting.
Monitor labor productivity and support cost-control initiatives.
Participate in forecasting manpower, equipment, and material needs.

Quality Management

Verify construction activities comply with drawings, specifications, and quality requirements.
Support inspections, testing, commissioning, and project turnover activities.
Help identify and resolve construction and engineering issues.

Safety Leadership

Promote and support Kiewit's safety culture.
Participate in job hazard analyses, pre-task planning, and field safety audits.
Ensure all work is performed in compliance with company, client, and regulatory requirements.

Client & Stakeholder Support

Interface with clients, inspectors, engineers, suppliers, and subcontractors.
Assist in coordinating project meetings, reporting, and issue resolution.
Maintain strong working relationships with project stakeholders.

Qualifications

Bachelor's degree in Civil, Electrical, Mechanical, Construction Engineering, or related field.
0-5+ years of construction, utility, power delivery, or industrial experience.
Strong interest in field construction and project execution.
Knowledge of transmission lines, substations, and utility infrastructure is preferred.
Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings and specifications.
Strong communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills.
Proficient with Microsoft Office and construction management software.
Other Requirements:
•    Regular, reliable attendance
•    Work productively and meet deadlines timely
•    Communicate and interact effectively and professionally with supervisors, employees, and others individually or in a team environment
•    Perform work safely and effectively. Understand and follow oral and written instructions, including warning signs, equipment use, and other policies.
•    Work during normal operating hours to organize and complete work within given deadlines. Work overtime and weekends as required.
•    FIELD ROLES ONLY May work at various different locations and conditions may vary

Base Compensation: $150,000/yr - $165,000/yr

(Actual compensation is subject to variation due to such factors as education, experience, skillset, and/or location)

