Position Overview
Kiewit is seeking an experienced Fiber Superintendent to lead field execution for fiber optic installation on a large-scale data center project. This role is responsible for overseeing all aspects of OSP and/or ISP fiber construction, driving safety, quality, and production across multiple crews and subcontractors.
The ideal candidate brings strong field leadership experience within telecommunications infrastructure and mission critical environments, with the ability to plan, coordinate, and execute complex fiber installation scopes while maintaining aggressive schedules and high-quality standards.District Overview
The Kiewit Industrial District delivers direct-hire construction services for complex industrial projects across the United States. Our work spans multiple sectors, including data centers, mineral processing, energy and water, with projects ranging from small capital work to major EPC projects.

We are committed to safety, quality, and excellence in execution, providing our clients with world-class solutions while offering our employees stability, growth, and career development opportunities within a multi-billion-dollar organization. Our culture is built on collaboration, innovation, integrity, and a shared passion for construction.

If you’re ready to take on complex, high-impact projects and make a lasting difference in the construction industry, the Kiewit Industrial District is where you can build a career that truly matters.Location
This role is based in Abilene, Texas. Responsibilities
Field Leadership & Execution

Provide direct oversight of OSP and ISP fiber installation crews, ensuring work is performed safely, efficiently, and in alignment with project requirements
Manage daily construction activities including conduit and innerduct installation

Fiber pulling and routing

Rack and cabinet installation
Fiber splicing and testing operations
Coordinate field activities across multiple crews to maintain production targets and schedule adherence

Safety, Quality & Compliance

Champion Kiewit’s safety-first culture, ensuring all work is executed in compliance with site safety standards and procedures
Conduct daily field walks, safety meetings, and job hazard analyses (JHAs)
Ensure all fiber installations meet quality standards, specifications, and client expectations, particularly in mission critical environments

Planning, Sequencing & Coordination

Develop and execute short-term and long-term work plans, ensuring proper sequencing of installation activities
Coordinate with general contractor, client stakeholders, and other trades to align schedules and avoid conflicts
Partner with project engineers and field engineers to ensure materials, equipment, and labor are aligned with project needs

Subcontractor Management

Oversee and manage subcontractor performance, ensuring adherence to contract scope, safety, and quality expectations
Track production, provide direction, and address performance gaps proactively
Ensure proper manpower planning and resource allocation to meet project milestones

Technical & Documentation Oversight

Interpret and execute work based on construction drawings, specifications, and design documents
Ensure accurate as-built documentation, redlines, and turnover packages are maintained
Support resolution of field issues, RFIs, and design clarifications
Qualifications
Required

7+ years of experience in fiber optic construction, with progressive leadership experience in the field
Proven experience leading OSP and/or ISP fiber installation crews

Strong working knowledge of:

Conduit and innerduct systems
Fiber installation, splicing, and testing
Data center fiber infrastructure (racks, pathways, patching)

Experience managing:

Daily construction activities and field execution
Manpower coordination and production tracking
Subcontractor oversight
Ability to read and interpret construction drawings and specifications
Strong communication skills with ability to coordinate across field teams, GC, and client stakeholders

Preferred

Experience working on large-scale data center or mission critical projects
Background in design-build or EPC environments
Familiarity with commissioning, turnover, and high-performance facility standards
OSHA certifications or equivalent safety training
